ret not mentioning them by name  it  for us very important to look at every  member state in the same way it is true  that with Hungary we have difficult  experiences so there will be a lot of  scrutiny but I think fairness among all  Member States is important and the  approach that we guarantee the  fundamental rights of the European Union  that we stand up being the guardian of  the treaty we have to be completely  neutral towards the Member State but  ready to act when something goes in the  wrong direction and here I'm very clear  what I said already that we're ready to  act the moment we see that the  implementation of these measures is not  appropriate as a trained physician when  you look at the situation that the world  is facing when you look at the situation  that the European Union is facing are  you sometimes just dismayed when you  look around this corona crisis is  devastating but it shows two sides it  shows on the one hand that there are  lessons we have to learn for example I  think we need a way more robust and  transparent data reporting system for us  in the European Union but also globally  to be better prepared and to have an  early warning system the second is that  we see how important is to have sound  strong health care systems that can  absorb shocks and that can respond to  crises like this one and the third one  that I think is important for the  European level is that we will have to  improve the system that the European  level is able to by critical medical  goods like personal protective equipment  like masks and Bluffs or ventilators buy  them stock pilot and distributed to  those Member States who need it this was  not in place at the beginning of the  crisis we put it in place now and we  will certainly have a very close look at  it the good part that we saw over the  last weeks is an enormous grow of  solidarity when I saw the the Polish and  the Romanian doctors and nurses going to  Italy  Italy on the other hand sharing test  kits with other the Member States France  sending patients to Germany and Austria  France sending masks to Spain and Italy  so many many examples of solidarity that  is and was good to see and I think later  on drawing the lessons from the crisis  this is on the positive side well we  thank you so much for joining us to  share that President of the European  Commission  Ursula founder line thank you so much
 

